setWorkflowSelectors
  ├── when the caller does not have the CONFIG_OPERATOR_ROLE
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when workflowId is zero
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__NoZeroWorkflowId
  ├── when selectors is empty
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__NoSelectors
  ├── when workflowId has no registered metadata
  │   ├── when the workflow was never registered
  │   │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__WorkflowNotRegistered
  │   └── when the workflow was registered and then removed
  │       └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__WorkflowNotRegistered
  ├── when called with a single selector
  │   ├── when isAllowlisted is true
  │   │   ├── it should set the selector as allowlisted
  │   │   └── it should emit a WorkflowSelectorSet event
  │   └── when isAllowlisted is false
  │       ├── it should remove the selector from the allowlist
  │       └── it should emit a WorkflowSelectorSet event
  ├── when called with multiple selectors
  │   └── it should set all selectors
  └── when setWorkflowMetadata is called after selectors were set
      └── it should no longer report the previously set selectors as allowlisted
